modulate = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
text = "EARTH PASS — INTERSTELLAR ENTRY AUTHORIZATION  
Terran Border & Hospitality Office, Sol‑III — Revision Gleep‑7

Pursuant to the Galactic Wanderer Safety & Snacking Act (GWSSA‑88), Section 4, Sub‑Clause 9‑Gleep, all non‑Terran entities seeking temporary presence within the Sol System must obtain an officially sanctioned EARTH PASS.

By accepting this document, the bearer acknowledges the following legally binding stipulations, codified under Terran Interplanetary Ordinance TIO‑12‑Blue:

The bearer agrees not to gleep, over‑gleep, or hyper‑gleep within 50 meters of any Terran government building, unless granted special ceremonial permission by an authorized Earthling wearing a reflective vest.

The bearer affirms that all appendages, visible or cloaked, are to remain in a non‑menacing configuration while interacting with Terran citizens, fauna, or vending machines.
Menacing configuration is defined as: wiggling, vibrating, humming, glowing, or attempting to purchase snacks without payment.

The bearer acknowledges Earth’s rotational schedule and agrees not to request manual adjustments to “slow the planet down a bit” for personal comfort.

The bearer accepts responsibility for any spontaneous atmospheric gleep‑echoes resulting from their presence. Terran authorities reserve the right to classify such echoes as “meteorological curiosities” or “mild inconveniences.”

The bearer consents to random friendliness checks, during which a Terran may approach and say “Hey, where you from?”
The bearer must respond truthfully, or at least with a fun fact about their home nebula.

The bearer agrees not to rearrange Earth’s continents, even if they believe “the vibes would be better if Australia were up top.”

The bearer understands that Earth snacks may cause temporary luminescence, particularly items labeled Extra Spicy, Flamin’, or Limited Edition Mystery Flavor.
Luminescence is normal.
Luminescence lasting more than 48 hours must be reported to the nearest Border Office or enthusiastic scientist.

The bearer acknowledges that Earth’s moon is not to be borrowed, even briefly, even “just to show the folks back home.”

The bearer agrees that any gleep‑based communication must be translated through an approved Terran Gleep‑Interpreter, unless the gleeping is purely recreational.

The bearer accepts that Earth is a Class‑3 Hospitality Planet, meaning Terrans may attempt to offer unsolicited beverages, directions, or life advice.
The bearer is not legally required to follow the advice.

By retaining this EARTH PASS, the bearer certifies compliance with all above clauses, sub‑clauses, and gleep‑adjacent regulations.  
Failure to comply may result in fines, stern looks, or being gently escorted back to orbit by a polite but firm satellite.

Welcome to Earth. Enjoy your stay, and please gleep responsibly."
